conductor-backup-selinux: SELinux policy for conductor-backup
=============================================================

The module "conductor_backup" (targeted policy, priority 200):

  conductor_backup_t        conductor-backup.service on a domain controller
                            (user conductor-backup)
  conductor_backup_drill_t  conductor-backup-drill.service on a drill host, set
                            by /usr/lib/systemd/system/conductor-backup-drill.service.d/selinux.conf;
                            an unconfined domain (the drill builds a network-less
                            sandbox with namespaces and mounts and runs samba-tool
                            restore and samba as root)

File types:

  conductor_backup_conf_t           /etc/conductor-backup (configuration, recipients)
  conductor_backup_cred_t           /etc/conductor-backup/credentials (read by systemd only)
  conductor_backup_var_lib_t        /var/lib/conductor-backup (spool, requests, policy)
  conductor_backup_drill_var_lib_t  /var/lib/conductor-backup-drill
  conductor_backup_store_t          /var/backups/conductor-backup (local destination)

On a domain controller, backups go through conductor-helper
(conductor_helper_t, from conductor-selinux), which this module lets write
the spool and read the recipients. conductor_backup_t uploads over HTTPS
(http_port_t: 443, 9000, ...) and sends alerts over SMTP. Another S3 port,
another local destination:

  semanage port -a -t http_port_t -p tcp 9900
  semanage fcontext -a -t conductor_backup_store_t '/srv/backups(/.*)?'
  restorecon -R /srv/backups

Troubleshooting:

  ausearch -m AVC,USER_AVC -ts recent -c conductor-backu
  semanage permissive -a conductor_backup_t     (and -d to revert)
